{{!
    @template mod_playerwords/round_play

    Guess submission trigger for an active round — the actual letter-by-letter entry
    happens in the grid itself (see mod_playerwords/round_panel), not here. game.js
    dynamically turns the grid's current (empty) row into one real single-character
    <input> per letter, mirroring mod_playercross's own tile-input pattern: clicking a
    specific box focuses exactly that one, so a wrong letter can be fixed without
    retyping the whole word — every other row (already played, or not yet reached)
    stays plain, non-interactive spans. Physical typing works even without a box
    focused, via game.js's document-level initPhysicalKeyboardCapture(); once a box
    does have native focus, ordinary typing/backspace/click-to-position all behave like
    a normal text field.

    This form exists purely as a submit-event target: game.js reads the guess by
    collecting every box's value from the active row when this form is submitted, via
    Enter or the on-screen keyboard's own ENTER key (both routed through the same
    submitGuessForm() helper — form.requestSubmit()). The visually-hidden submit button
    below is the discoverable action for keyboard/screen-reader users; sighted/mouse
    users never see it, since the whole flow already works via typing.

    The on-screen keyboard itself is a sibling in mod_playerwords/round_panel, not here,
    so it keeps sharing that template's own (tall) containing block for
    position: sticky — see round_panel's docblock for why. Since #playerwords-round-play
    is what game.js's showRoundResult() replaces wholesale when the round finishes, the
    keyboard living outside it means that function also removes the keyboard node
    explicitly, so it never lingers orphaned on the result screen.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "submitguess": "Submit guess"
    }
}}
<div id="playerwords-round-play">
    <form id="playerwords-guess-form" class="mod-playerwords-form">
        <button type="submit" class="visually-hidden">{{submitguess}}</button>
    </form>
</div>
